From d802042d314faf9c150c53c9ff6c803a7542333b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:26:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Tilespec: whole-tile terrain with two match types picks a
 second variant set next to the second type

A whole-tile layer with layer<n>_match_with naming one other match type
(MATCH_PAIR) was "Not yet defined" and asserted. It now loads two
variant sets: t.l<n>.<tag>1 and up as before, and t.l<n>.<tag>_<type>1
and up, drawn on a tile that has a tile of the second match type among
its eight neighbours (whole_variant()). Freeciv45 uses it for cool pine
on forest next to tundra and glacier.

In overhead view such a terrain also fades into its neighbours from the
pair set where it is drawn with it (blend_pair), and the variant fades of
patch 0028 treat the two sets as one list of variants.
---
 client/tilespec.c | 170 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 148 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/client/tilespec.c b/client/tilespec.c
index 2c14579..f9f602b 100644
--- a/client/tilespec.c
+++ b/client/tilespec.c
